2026-05-05T09:35:18.685Z {"session_id":"ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ecbabb33-c3c8-42cb-9008-6feb0556cea4.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"## ✅ LightRAG Migration Complete\n\nThe platform has been successfully migrated from **Qdrant + Ollama** to **LightRAG** with GPT-4.1-nano. Here's what changed:\n\n---\n\n## 🎯 What Was Changed\n\n### **New Files**\n1. **`app/services/lightrag_service.py`** — Central LightRAG instance with:\n   - `gpt41_nano_complete()` — async LLM function using OpenAI SDK\n   - `openai_embed()` — async embedding function (text-embedding-3-small, 1536-dim)\n   - `search_docs()` — hybrid graph+vector retrieval with `only_need_context=True`\n   - `insert_text()` — adds structured text blocks to the knowledge graph\n   - `initialize()` — called from FastAPI lifespan\n\n2. **`requirements.txt`** — Dependencies documented:\n   - `lightrag-hku`, `openai`, `fastapi`, `pypdf`, `python-docx`, etc.\n\n### **Modified Files**\n\n| File | Changes |\n|---|---|\n| `app/main.py` | Added `lifespan` context manager calling `lightrag_service.initialize()` |\n| `app/services/rag.py` | Now a thin wrapper delegating to `lightrag_service.search_docs()` |\n| `ingestion/ingest.py` | Replaced Qdrant upsert with `lightrag_service.insert_text()` per situation block; removed `get_embedding()`, `ensure_collection()`, `recreate_collection()` |\n| `app/services/llm_service.py` | Updated system prompt `<rules>` to mention graph-sourced context and LightRAG |\n| `docker-compose.yml` | Removed Qdrant and Ollama services (no longer needed) |\n| `CLAUDE.md` | Updated all architecture & setup docs to reflect LightRAG |\n\n### **Unchanged**\n- `app/routers/chat.py` — Entity detection & query enrichment logic preserved\n- `app/services/validation.py`, `rate_limit.py`, `rulebased.py`, `task_queue.py`\n- Frontend and static files\n\n---\n\n## 🚀 How It Works Now\n\n### **Retrieval Pipeline**\n```\nUser message \n  → Language detection (RU/KZ)\n  → Entity detection (FL/UL)\n  → Query enrichment: [intent] [entity] {message}\n  → LightRAG hybrid search:\n     • Extracts entities from documents (gpt-4.1-nano)\n     • Builds knowledge graph (NetworkX)\n     • Retrieves via graph traversal + vector similarity\n     • Returns raw context\n  → ask_llm() with language rules & formatting\n  → Response with bold buttons, steps, Kazakh translation\n```\n\n### **Knowledge Graph Storage**\n- **Location**: `./data/lightrag/`\n- **Format**: NetworkX graph + nano-vectordb (local, embedded)\n- **Embeddings**: text-embedding-3-small (1536-dim)\n- **Entity extraction**: gpt-4.1-nano (automatic during ingestion)\n- **Query mode**: `\"hybrid\"` (graph relations + vector similarity)\n\n### **Ingestion Strategy**\nEach document is parsed into situation-level blocks:\n```\n[FILENAME: doc.docx] [INTENT: tu_application] [LANGUAGE: ru] [TITLE: Ситуация 1]\n{situation description + answer template}\n```\n\nLightRAG automatically:\n- Chunks by 1200-token blocks\n- Extracts entities & relationships\n- Builds incrementally (no full wipe on re-ingest)\n- Stores all data locally\n\n---\n\n## ⚙️ Setup & Running\n\n### **One-time Install**\n```bash\npip install -r requirements.txt\n```\n\n### **Environment Setup**\n```bash\n# .env\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-your-key-here\nLLM_PROVIDER=openai\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-nano\n```\n\n### **Start the App**\n```bash\nuvicorn app.main:app --reload --port 8001\n```\n\n### **Ingest Documents**\n```bash\npython ingestion/ingest.py\n```\n\n---\n\n## 📊 Key Improvements\n\n| Aspect | Before (Qdrant) | After (LightRAG) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Retrieval | Dense vector search | Graph + vectors (hybrid) |\n| Dependencies | Qdrant + Ollama services | Local embeddings + graph |\n| Entity extraction | Manual chunking | Automatic (LLM-driven) |\n| Relationships | None tracked | Full knowledge graph |\n| API cost | None (self-hosted) | ~$0.50–$2 per 100KB (entity extraction) |\n| Setup complexity | Docker Compose + Ollama | Just `pip install` + `OPENAI_API_KEY` |\n| Incremental ingestion | Collection wipe on each run | Additive (keeps existing graph) |\n\n---\n\n## ⚠️ Important Notes\n\n1. **Knowledge graph is local** — `./data/lightrag/` is persistent. Back it up if important.\n2. **Deleting a document via API** does NOT remove its nodes from the graph. Re-index if you need to fully remove content.\n3. **LightRAG makes LLM calls** during ingestion (gpt-4.1-nano for entity extraction). Monitor costs if ingesting large volumes.\n4. **Language handling** is still in `ask_llm()` — Kazakh responses, formatting, and rules are unchanged.\n5. **Entity detection in chat.py** is unchanged — FL/UL detection flows directly into the enriched query.\n\n---\n\n## ✨ What's Better\n\n- **Smarter retrieval** — Relationships between iSEL concepts (steps, buttons, user types, situations) are now understood by the graph\n- **Fewer external services** — No Docker, no Ollama, no Qdrant — just OpenAI API\n- **Cost-effective** — GPT-4.1-nano is cheap, and OpenAI embeddings are fast\n- **Language-aware** — Knowledge graph captures Russian AND Kazakh entity relationships\n- **Maintained locally** — Full control over the graph; no cloud dependency except OpenAI API\n\nReady to ingest your first document and test the new graph-based retrieval! 🎉"}

