2026-05-12T07:20:26.920Z {"session_id":"9fbbc20f-0fdc-4c8b-aa85-9b48cf5d424e","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\9fbbc20f-0fdc-4c8b-aa85-9b48cf5d424e.jsonl","cwd":"E:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"**49/49 tests passing. Committed.**\n\n---\n\n## What was done and why\n\n### Architecture problems fixed\n\n| Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|\n| `is_entity_fix` + `step is None + entity` overlap | Single path in `LinearFlow.next_state()` — one condition, deterministic |\n| `situation` field never read/written | Kept in `FlowState` for future use, removed dead code in router |\n| No FAQ interruption during locked flow | `update_history_only()` answers FAQ without touching flow state |\n| Entity dropped from enriched query when history present | `_annotate_question()` always appends entity to LLM input |\n| Monolithic `chat.py` with 10+ inline helpers | Thin router, all flow logic in `app/flows/` |\n| Prompt rebuilt + all blocks sent every request | Static `_STATIC_PROMPT_RU/KZ` prefix for OpenAI caching; dynamic blocks only appended when non-empty |\n\n### New structure\n\n```\napp/flows/\n  base.py       ← FlowContext dataclass + BaseFlow interface\n  linear.py     ← TU: step 1-5, entity gate, capped at MAX_STEPS\n  scenario.py   ← Real Estate: last-turn context in query\n  faq.py        ← passthrough, no state tracking\n  registry.py   ← get_flow(), classify_intent(), has_flow_keywords()\n\napp/services/\n  session.py    ← SessionManager with 3 update modes\n\ntests/\n  test_flows.py   ← 36 tests (step progression, final step, transitions, registry)\n  test_session.py ← 13 tests (state, history, FAQ interruption, cleanup)\n```\n\n### FAQ interruption — how it works now\n\nIf a user is in TU step 3 and asks \"как зарегистрироваться?\":\n1. `state.locked=True` + no flow keywords + not \"дальше\" → FAQ interruption detected\n2. Routes through `FAQFlow`, queries LightRAG without intent/step prefix\n3. Calls `update_history_only()` — history records the exchange, step stays at 3\n4. Next message resumes TU at step 3 normally"}

