2026-05-13T09:30:16.048Z {"session_id":"ca3f5120-e675-4699-ba4c-7a0236bf3ad3","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ca3f5120-e675-4699-ba4c-7a0236bf3ad3.jsonl","cwd":"E:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"50/50. Summary of what was done and why it differs from the proposal:\n\n**Fix 1 — root cause was different from the proposal's analysis**\n\nThe proposal traced a history-walk failure and concluded \"SOMETHING ELSE IS WRONG\" — it was right. The actual bug: `update_state_only` (called by the clarification gate on Turn 1) saves no history entry. On Turn 2 when \"жт\" arrives, `history = []`, so the walk finds nothing and returns `\"ru\"`.\n\nThe fix: add `_KZ_ENTITY_EXACT` (`{\"жт\", \"зт\", \"ж.т.\", \"з.т.\"}`) and check it before the history walk in `_detect_language` ([chat.py:51-68](app/routers/chat.py#L51-L68)). These tokens are exclusively Kazakh entity abbreviations in this platform — no context needed.\n\nThe proposed whitelist (`\"да\"`, `\"нет\"`, `\"бар\"`) was rejected because `\"да\"`/`\"нет\"` are Russian words and would incorrectly force KZ detection for Russian speakers. `\"ия\"`/`\"жок\"` were already handled — translit converts them to `\"иә\"`/`\"жоқ\"` which have KZ chars before `_detect_language` is even called.\n\n**Fix 2 — accepted as proposed, test updated**\n\nBare `\"кадастр\"` removed from `INTENT_KEYWORDS`; replaced with `\"кадастровый номер\"`, `\"через кадастр\"`, `\"по кадастру\"` ([registry.py:23-32](app/flows/registry.py#L23-L32)). Test `test_re_keywords` updated to assert `\"кадастр\"` no longer triggers, `\"кадастровый номер\"` does ([test_flows.py:190-193](tests/test_flows.py#L190-L193)).\n\n**Fix 3 — not implemented** (no-op: translit already doesn't map `\"жт\"`, and Fix 1 makes it unnecessary)."}

2026-05-13T09:47:57.735Z {"session_id":"ca3f5120-e675-4699-ba4c-7a0236bf3ad3","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ca3f5120-e675-4699-ba4c-7a0236bf3ad3.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","hook_event_name":"UserPromptSubmit","prompt":"# Fix: real_estate flow should NOT require entity (ЖТ/ЗТ) clarification\n# The document \"Добавление объекта недвижимости\" has no ФЛ/ЮЛ branching —\n# all 5 situations apply equally to individuals and legal entities.\n\n# ---- chat.py: update _needs_entity_clarification ----\npython << 'PYEOF'\nwith open(\"app/routers/chat.py\", \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nold = '''def _needs_entity_clarification(\n    intent: Optional[str], entity: Optional[str], page: Optional[str]\n) -> bool:\n    if entity is not None:\n        return False\n    if intent not in (\"real_estate\", \"tu_application\"):\n        return False\n    # Shared steps (2–5) work the same for both entity types — skip gate\n    if page and any(step in page.lower() for step in _SHARED_STEPS):\n        return False\n    return True'''\n\nnew = '''def _needs_entity_clarification(\n    intent: Optional[str], entity: Optional[str], page: Optional[str]\n) -> bool:\n    if entity is not None:\n        return False\n    # Only TU application requires entity clarification (ФЛ/ЮЛ have different forms).\n    # Real estate object addition works identically for all user types.\n    if intent != \"tu_application\":\n        return False\n    # Shared steps (2–5) work the same for both entity types — skip gate\n    if page and any(step in page.lower() for step in _SHARED_STEPS):\n        return False\n    return True'''\n\ncontent = content.replace(old, new)\nwith open(\"app/routers/chat.py\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\nprint(\"chat.py: _needs_entity_clarification — real_estate removed from entity gate\")\nPYEOF\n\n# ---- Also: real_estate in ScenarioFlow should not require entity ----\npython << 'PYEOF'\nwith open(\"app/flows/scenario.py\", \"r\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    content = f.read()\n\nold = \"    requires_entity = True\"\nnew = \"    requires_entity = False  # Real estate process is identical for ФЛ/ЮЛ\"\n\ncontent = content.replace(old, new)\nwith open(\"app/flows/scenario.py\", \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n    f.write(content)\nprint(\"scenario.py: requires_entity = False for ScenarioFlow\")\nPYEOF\n\n# ---- Run tests ----\npython -m pytest tests/ -v"}

