2026-05-13T19:27:37.762Z {"session_id":"ca3f5120-e675-4699-ba4c-7a0236bf3ad3","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\ca3f5120-e675-4699-ba4c-7a0236bf3ad3.jsonl","cwd":"E:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"55/55. Here's what was fixed and why the proposed approach was adjusted:\n\n**Bug 1 — `situation` never set ([scenario.py](app/flows/scenario.py))**  \n`next_state()` now detects situation keywords in the message. When found, it appends the user's answer to `original_question` so `build_query` automatically includes \"кадастр\" in the RAG query on the next turn — no separate change to `build_query` needed. Once `situation` is set, it's never overwritten (`if ctx.state.situation is not None: return model_copy()`).\n\n**Bug 2 — locking never fires for real_estate ([chat.py:240-246](app/routers/chat.py#L240-L246))**  \nThe condition `state.entity is not None` was wrong for real_estate (we removed entity clarification). New condition: TU locks when `entity + step` are set; real_estate locks when `situation` is set.\n\n**Bug 3 — RAG query missing \"кадастр\"**  \nSolved as a side-effect of Bug 1: when situation is detected, `original_question` is updated to include the user's answer before `build_query` runs (chat.py rebuilds `ctx` with the post-`next_state` state).\n\n**Latent bug 4 — \"кадастр аркылы\" wouldn't normalize**  \nAdded `\"аркылы\"` → `\"арқылы\"` and `\"адрестик регистр\"` → `\"адрестік регистр\"` to [translit.py](app/services/translit.py). Also added `\"кадастр арқылы\"` and `\"адресный регистр\"` / `\"адрестік регистр\"` to [registry.py INTENT_KEYWORDS](app/flows/registry.py#L23-L32) so `has_flow_keywords` recognises them — prevents FAQ-interruption misfires once the flow is locked."}

