2026-05-14T11:36:20.878Z {"session_id":"7439697e-8f68-4e46-bc41-ecc4eba22aa6","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\7439697e-8f68-4e46-bc41-ecc4eba22aa6.jsonl","cwd":"E:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","effort":{"level":"medium"},"hook_event_name":"Stop","stop_hook_active":false,"last_assistant_message":"57/57 clean. Summary of what changed:\n\n**`llm_service.py` — TU intent (both RU and KZ):** Added a `ПРИОРИТЕТ`/`БАСЫМДЫҚ` rule as the absolute first bullet. When the user asks about status or downloading documents it fires immediately with the navigation path only, before the navigation-at-top rule, entity rules, and step logic even get evaluated.\n\n**`llm_service.py` — real estate RULE 1 (both RU and KZ):** Added an explicit one-liner prohibiting listing steps for both ways in a single answer — just the clarifying question.\n\n**`chat.py` — `_safe_normalize_kz`:** Wraps `normalize_kz`. If the input had no KZ chars but normalization introduced them (e.g. \"тех условие\" → \"техникалық шарттар\") AND the original contains Russian function words (\"где\", \"как\", \"что\", \"я\", \"мой\", \"подал\", …), the result is reverted to the original message. `_detect_language` then sees no KZ chars and correctly returns `\"ru\"`. The guard uses whole-word matching (space-padded) to avoid false positives inside longer strings."}

2026-05-14T11:47:38.370Z {"session_id":"7439697e-8f68-4e46-bc41-ecc4eba22aa6","transcript_path":"C:\\Users\\yasmi\\.claude\\projects\\e--workstuff-platform-ai-assistant\\7439697e-8f68-4e46-bc41-ecc4eba22aa6.jsonl","cwd":"e:\\workstuff\\platform_ai_assistant","permission_mode":"acceptEdits","hook_event_name":"UserPromptSubmit","prompt":"IMPORTANT:\n- Do NOT blindly follow my implementation suggestions.\n- First identify architectural problems, hidden bugs, regressions, duplicated logic, and better alternatives.\n- If my proposed solution is suboptimal, explain why and implement a safer/better approach.\n- Preserve backward compatibility whenever possible.\n- Avoid overengineering.\n- Keep changes modular and maintainable.\n- After implementation, RUN TESTS and fix regressions until everything passes.\n\nВ app/routers/chat.py добавить проверку навигационных FAQ-запросов.\n\nРасположение: после intent classification, до entity detection и clarification gate.\n\nЛогика:\n- Определить список NAVIGATION_TRIGGERS — слова указывающие что пользователь\n  хочет найти/посмотреть/скачать, а не заполнять форму:\n  \"статус\", \"посмотреть\", \"где\", \"скачать\", \"документ\", \"готовое\", \"найти\", \"проверить\"\n- После строки `new_intent = classify_intent(...)` добавить:\n  Если сообщение содержит любой из NAVIGATION_TRIGGERS И при этом НЕ содержит\n  слова явно указывающие на заполнение (\"заполнить\", \"шаг\", \"подать\", \"создать\") —\n  вернуть навигационный ответ из <navigation_facts> через ask_llm с intent=None\n  (как FAQ), без прохождения clarification gate и flow.\n\n- Ответ должен использовать правило 13 из промпта (navigation_facts) + контекст из RAG.\n- Сессию обновлять через sessions.update_history_only чтобы не сломать flow\n  если пользователь вернётся к заполнению.\n\nДля казахского языка аналогичные триггеры:\n\"мәртебе\", \"күй\", \"қайда\", \"қарау\", \"жүктеу\", \"дайын\", \"табу\", \"тексеру\"\n\npython -m pytest tests/ -v после правки."}

